WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.298
Hi, I'm Fillet!

00:00:02.298 --> 00:00:04.984
An industrial geometry kernel just went open source.

00:00:04.984 --> 00:00:08.007
Here is how a kernel keeps a solid exact.

00:00:10.475 --> 00:00:12.204
A mesh is just triangles.

00:00:12.204 --> 00:00:16.354
A kernel's solid is exact surfaces plus topology: which trimmed pieces are

00:00:16.354 --> 00:00:18.083
kept, and which ones touch.

00:00:21.008 --> 00:00:24.836
A model splits space into regions, solid and void, each bounded by

00:00:24.836 --> 00:00:26.112
a shell of faces.

00:00:26.532 --> 00:00:29.779
A face is a piece of an exact surface: a plane, a

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:31.133
cylinder, or a spline patch.

00:00:31.553 --> 00:00:33.680
Loops of edges say which part is kept.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.806
Outer loops run one way, holes the other.

00:00:36.226 --> 00:00:39.744
Every edge carries an exact curve and knows each face it bounds.

00:00:41.675 --> 00:00:44.875
Every time a face, loop or edge bounds something, that incidence

00:00:44.875 --> 00:00:46.039
is its own use.

00:00:46.039 --> 00:00:48.075
A face has two, one per side.

00:00:48.495 --> 00:00:52.155
So one edge can bound three or four faces mid boolean, which

00:00:52.155 --> 00:00:53.375
simpler structures cannot hold.

00:00:54.775 --> 00:00:56.980
A boolean runs in four careful phases.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.328
Find every place the two solids meet, in scratch space.

00:01:00.748 --> 00:01:03.987
Merge pieces within tolerance, and stop if anything failed.

00:01:04.407 --> 00:01:06.918
Only then imprint the cuts into the real solids.

00:01:07.338 --> 00:01:11.616
Classify each face as inside or outside, and keep what the operation wants.

00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:17.028
Today, design data becomes triangles before it enters the scene graph.

00:01:17.448 --> 00:01:22.196
The new schema stores topology as flat index arrays, with exact surfaces beside it.

00:01:23.717 --> 00:01:26.791
And the kernel is no toy: nearly a million lines of code.

00:01:30.642 --> 00:01:33.715
Within a day, outside developers had fixed real bugs.

00:01:33.715 --> 00:01:37.472
Open means anyone can read, fix and embed the hard parts.

00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:42.358
Exact surfaces, explicit neighbours, and solids in the scene graph.

00:01:42.358 --> 00:01:43.674
See you next time!

00:01:44.094 --> 00:01:46.212
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:46.212 --> 00:01:46.817
I'm Fillet.

00:01:46.817 --> 00:01:47.119
Bye!
